# ============================================================================
# .gitignore for an Unreal Engine project
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to the ROOT of your Unreal project (next to your .uproject)
# and RENAME it to exactly ".gitignore" (with the leading dot).
# It keeps all of Unreal's generated/build files out of the repo so teammates
# only sync source + assets, not gigabytes of machine-specific junk.
# ============================================================================

# --- Unreal generated folders (never commit these) --------------------------
Binaries/
Build/
DerivedDataCache/
Intermediate/
Saved/
Script/
.vs/

# Some teams DO want to keep default config. If so, delete the next line.
# By default we keep the project Config folder (it is small text and important):
!Config/

# Plugin generated folders
Plugins/**/Binaries/
Plugins/**/Intermediate/

# --- IDE / editor files -----------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
*.VC.db
*.VC.opendb
*.opensdf
*.opendb
*.sdf
*.suo
*.sln
*.xcodeproj/
*.xcworkspace/
.DS_Store

# --- Compiled binaries ------------------------------------------------------
*.exe
*.dll
*.dylib
*.so
*.o
*.obj
*.pdb
*.lib
*.a

# --- Packaged / cooked builds (usually huge, ship separately) ---------------
[Bb]uild/
[Bb]uilds/
Cooked/
Packaged/

# --- Crash / log artifacts --------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.tlog
*.stackdump

# --- OS junk ----------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
